<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <!--
    Nop.Plugin.ExchangeRate.EcbExchange - task 10.3.

    ===================================================================================
    THE VIEWLESS VARIANT OF THE PLUGIN RECIPE. The full recipe and its reasoning live in
    src/Plugins/Nop.Plugin.DiscountRules.CustomerRoles/Nop.Plugin.DiscountRules.CustomerRoles.csproj
    (task 10.1).
    ===================================================================================
    This plugin ships NO .cshtml, no controller and no IRouteProvider - it is one class
    implementing IExchangeRateProvider, configured from the admin currency settings page rather
    than from a page of its own. So two of the four load-bearing decisions do not apply and the
    SDK is different:

      * Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk", NOT Microsoft.NET.Sdk.Razor, and no AddRazorSupportForMvc.
        There is nothing to compile as Razor and nothing to contribute as a Razor application
        part. Same choice as src/Tests/Nop.Plugin.SmokeProbe (task 8.8).
        FOR GROUPS 11-15: the SDK depends on whether the plugin has views. Of the 20 plugins,
        this is the ONLY one with none (verified: `find . -name "*.cshtml"` over
        src/Plugins/ returns 38 files across the other 19 projects). Every other plugin needs
        Microsoft.NET.Sdk.Razor + AddRazorSupportForMvc=true.
      * No Content/Link block, and no Views/_ViewImports.cshtml - and note that this plugin
        never had a web.config either, precisely because it has no views. There was nothing to
        transcribe.

    The other two DO apply, unchanged and for the same reasons:

      * OutputPath = ..\..\Presentation\Nop.Web\Plugins\ExchangeRate.EcbExchange\ with
        AppendTargetFrameworkToOutputPath=false. PluginManager scans ~/Plugins for
        Description.txt and IsPackagePluginFolder requires the containing folder's PARENT to be
        named "Plugins", so an appended net10.0 segment makes the plugin invisible.
      * Private="false" on both ProjectReferences PLUS the
        NopPluginDoNotDeployHostAssemblies target: a Nop.*.dll deployed next to a plugin gets
        shadow-copied and loaded by PluginManager as the process's copy of that assembly.

    No FrameworkReference: nothing here binds an ASP.NET Core type. Nop.Core and Nop.Services
    declare Microsoft.AspNetCore.App themselves and it flows transitively for compilation, so
    restating it would add nothing.

    DROPPED in the classic -> SDK conversion, the same list as 10.1 minus the Razor pieces:
    the MSBuild 2003 scaffolding and ProjectGuid {6DF00C56-EC49-4AB8-8B29-404E3694026C}; the
    Debug/Release PropertyGroup pair; the explicit <Compile> list of 2 files; the
    Microsoft.CSharp.targets import, the BeforeBuild/AfterBuild stubs, the
    Microsoft.Bcl.Build.targets import and its EnsureNuGetPackageBuildImports guard; every
    <Reference> (BCL entries subsumed by net10.0, System.Web with no counterpart, and the
    packages\ HintPath entries for the MVC 5 / WebPages / Bcl.Async / Net.Http packages);
    app.config (a <runtime>/<assemblyBinding> block of .NET Framework binding redirects, which
    do not exist on .NET) and packages.config (central package management is in force).

    KEPT: Properties/AssemblyInfo.cs - src/Directory.Build.props sets
    GenerateAssemblyInfo=false, so deleting it would drop AssemblyVersion to 0.0.0.0.

    ONE WARNING IS EXPECTED AND IS DELIBERATELY NOT FIXED. EcbExchangeRateProvider.cs uses
    WebRequest.Create/HttpWebRequest, which is SYSLIB0014-obsolete on net10.0 ("use HttpClient
    instead"). The code still works; rewriting it against HttpClient would be a behavioural
    rewrite of the plugin's only method, which is outside a port. This is exactly how the same
    API was treated in Nop.Core (OfficialFeedManager), Nop.Services (KeepAliveTask) and
    Nop.Admin (task 8.3 recorded its two sites as "pre-existing 3.90 code newly unmasked").
    Recorded as deferral 10.3-1.
  -->

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <OutputPath>..\..\Presentation\Nop.Web\Plugins\ExchangeRate.EcbExchange\</OutputPath>
    <AppendTargetFrameworkToOutputPath>false</AppendTargetFrameworkToOutputPath>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\Libraries\Nop.Core\Nop.Core.csproj" Private="false" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\Libraries\Nop.Services\Nop.Services.csproj" Private="false" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <!-- see 10.1: the Private metadata alone leaks the transitive Nop.Data.dll -->
  <Target Name="NopPluginDoNotDeployHostAssemblies" AfterTargets="ResolveReferences">
    <ItemGroup>
      <ReferenceCopyLocalPaths
          Remove="@(ReferenceCopyLocalPaths)"
          Condition="$([System.String]::Copy('%(Filename)').StartsWith('Nop.'))" />
    </ItemGroup>
  </Target>

  <!--
    Include, not Update. Under the plain Microsoft.NET.Sdk there are no default Content items at
    all, so .txt/.jpg arrive as <None>; the <None Remove> keeps each file in one item type.
    Description.txt must be deployed or PluginManager cannot see the plugin, and its
    SupportedVersions list must contain NopVersion.CurrentVersion ("3.90").
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <None Remove="Description.txt" />
    <None Remove="logo.jpg" />
    <None Remove="Notes.txt" />
    <Content Include="Description.txt" CopyToOutputDirectory="PreserveNewest" />
    <Content Include="logo.jpg" CopyToOutputDirectory="Always" />
    <Content Include="Notes.txt" CopyToOutputDirectory="Never" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
